IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 12E and 12F -- keeping a director's, chief executive officer's, secretary's or private-company member's residential address
-- out of public access, and the notice, representations, appeal and three-year bar that go with ending that protection. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- The Registrar and the Court appear only as the holders of powers and duties over the individual; there is no seat for them.
-- The heading of s 12E says "if contact address is available", but subsection (1) states no such condition (finding in NOTES.md); the functions follow the text of the subsections.
--
-- Answers. `JUST TRUE` is yes; `JUST FALSE` is the text saying no in its own words; `NOTHING` is "the text does not say".
-- Periods are counted only by sg-periods.l4. "within N days after X" in a duty or a right is read here as: X itself is in time (fork line F-H-P2 in NOTES.md).

§ `Section 12E: exclusion of the residential address from public access`

-- src:3218 | 12E.—(1) The Registrar must cause —
-- src:3220 | (a) the residential address of a director, chief executive officer
-- src:3221 | or secretary contained in the register of directors, register
-- src:3222 | of chief executive officers or register of secretaries (as the
-- src:3223 | case may be) kept by the Registrar under section 173(1) to
-- src:3224 | be excluded from public access under section 12(2)(c); and
-- src:3228 | (b) the residential address of a member of a private company
-- src:3229 | (who is an individual) contained in the electronic register
-- src:3230 | of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A to be
-- src:3231 | excluded from public access under section 12(2)(d).
@ref s 12E(1) (src:3218-3231)
GIVEN `the address is the residential address of a director, chief executive officer or secretary of a company contained in the register of directors, register of chief executive officers or register of secretaries kept by the Registrar under section 173(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is the residential address of a member of a private company, who is an individual, contained in the electronic register of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12E(1) the Registrar must cause the residential address to be excluded from public access` MEANS
    IF    `the address is the residential address of a director, chief executive officer or secretary of a company contained in the register of directors, register of chief executive officers or register of secretaries kept by the Registrar under section 173(1)`
       OR `the address is the residential address of a member of a private company, who is an individual, contained in the electronic register of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "the residential address of a director, chief executive officer or secretary" in the registers kept under section 173(1) and of "a member of a private company (who is an individual)" in the register kept under section 196A; the text says nothing of any other address

-- (2): "Where, pursuant to subsection (1) or (3), the residential address ... is excluded from public access ..., the Registrar may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded ... in accordance with section 12F."
-- A grant gated by "Where": JUST FALSE when the address is not so excluded (periods ruling (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1); "in accordance with section 12F" limits it (NOTHING: fork line F-H-S3).
-- src:3235 | (2) Where, pursuant to subsection (1) or (3), the residential address
-- src:3236 | of a director, chief executive officer or secretary of a company or a
-- src:3237 | member of a private company mentioned in subsection (1) (called in
-- src:3238 | this section and section 12F the individual) is excluded from public
-- src:3239 | access under section 12(2)(c) or (d) (as the case may be), the Registrar
-- src:3240 | may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded from such
-- src:3241 | public access in accordance with section 12F.
@ref s 12E(2) (src:3235-3241)
GIVEN `the residential address of the individual is excluded from public access under section 12(2)(c) or (d) pursuant to subsection (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has proceeded in accordance with section 12F` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12E(2) the Registrar may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the residential address of the individual is excluded from public access under section 12(2)(c) or (d) pursuant to subsection (1) or (3)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, pursuant to subsection (1) or (3), the residential address ... is excluded from public access under section 12(2)(c) or (d) ..., the Registrar may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1)
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar has proceeded in accordance with section 12F`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "in accordance with section 12F"; the text says nothing of an exercise that is not (fork line F-H-S3)

-- src:3245 | (3) Where, pursuant to subsection (2), the individual’s residential
-- src:3246 | address has ceased to be excluded from public access under
-- src:3251 | section 12(2)(c) or (d) (as the case may be), the Registrar must cause
-- src:3252 | the exclusion from public access to resume if —
-- src:3254 | (a) subject to section 12F(8) and the equivalent provisions in
-- src:3255 | other ACRA administered Acts, notice of a change in the
-- src:3256 | individual’s contact address is lodged under any ACRA
-- src:3257 | administered Act; or
-- src:3259 | (b) the Court so directs on an appeal under section 12F(7).
@ref s 12E(3) (src:3245-3259)
GIVEN `the residential address of the individual has ceased to be excluded from public access under section 12(2)(c) or (d) pursuant to subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of a change in the individual's contact address is lodged under an ACRA administered Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 12F(8), or an equivalent provision in another ACRA administered Act, bars the lodging` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has directed that the exclusion resume, on an appeal under section 12F(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12E(3) the Registrar must cause the exclusion from public access to resume` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the residential address of the individual has ceased to be excluded from public access under section 12(2)(c) or (d) pursuant to subsection (2)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, pursuant to subsection (2), the individual's residential address has ceased to be excluded from public access ..., the Registrar must cause the exclusion from public access to resume if" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); a duty's own question)
    ELSE (IF (`notice of a change in the individual's contact address is lodged under an ACRA administered Act` AND (NOT `section 12F(8), or an equivalent provision in another ACRA administered Act, bars the lodging`)) OR `the Court has directed that the exclusion resume, on an appeal under section 12F(7)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must cause the exclusion from public access to resume if -- (a) subject to section 12F(8) and the equivalent provisions in other ACRA administered Acts, notice of a change in the individual's contact address is lodged under any ACRA administered Act; or (b) the Court so directs on an appeal under section 12F(7)" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- src:3263 | (4) Where —
-- src:3265 | (a) a document is filed or lodged with the Registrar under this
-- src:3266 | Act by submitting a form on the electronic transaction
-- src:3267 | system on or after the date of commencement of section 30
-- src:3268 | of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements)
-- src:3269 | Act 2024; and
-- src:3271 | (b) an individual’s residential address is entered in that form,
-- src:3273 | the Registrar must cause the individual’s residential address to be
-- src:3274 | excluded from public access in respect of that document under
-- src:3275 | section 12(2)(b).
@ref s 12E(4) (src:3263-3275)
GIVEN `the document was filed or lodged with the Registrar under this Act by submitting a form on the electronic transaction system on or after the date of commencement of section 30 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an individual's residential address is entered in that form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12E(4) the Registrar must cause the residential address to be excluded from public access in respect of the document` MEANS
    IF `the document was filed or lodged with the Registrar under this Act by submitting a form on the electronic transaction system on or after the date of commencement of section 30 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024` AND `an individual's residential address is entered in that form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where -- (a) a document is filed or lodged with the Registrar ... by submitting a form on the electronic transaction system on or after the date of commencement of section 30 ...; and (b) an individual's residential address is entered in that form, the Registrar must cause the individual's residential address to be excluded" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); a duty's own question)

§ `Section 12F: ending the exclusion, and the individual's protections`

-- (1): the grounds "are either that (a) ...; or (b) ...": a closed list ("either"), so neither is JUST FALSE.
-- src:3283 | 12F.—(1) For the purposes of section 12E(2), the grounds for
-- src:3284 | causing the individual’s residential address to cease to be excluded
-- src:3285 | from public access under section 12(2)(c) or (d) (as the case may be)
-- src:3286 | are either that —
-- src:3288 | (a) communications sent by the Registrar under this Act, or by
-- src:3289 | any officer of the Authority under any ACRA administered
-- src:3290 | Act, to the individual at his or her contact address and
-- src:3291 | requiring a response within a specified period remain
-- src:3292 | unanswered; or
-- src:3294 | (b) there is evidence to show that service of any document
-- src:3295 | under this Act or under any ACRA administered Act at the
-- src:3300 | individual’s contact address is not effective to bring it to
-- src:3301 | the notice of the individual.
@ref s 12F(1) (src:3283-3301)
GIVEN `communications sent by the Registrar under this Act, or by an officer of the Authority under an ACRA administered Act, to the individual at the contact address and requiring a response within a specified period remain unanswered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to show that service of a document under this Act or an ACRA administered Act at the individual's contact address is not effective to bring it to the notice of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(1) a ground exists for causing the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` MEANS
    IF    `communications sent by the Registrar under this Act, or by an officer of the Authority under an ACRA administered Act, to the individual at the contact address and requiring a response within a specified period remain unanswered`
       OR `there is evidence to show that service of a document under this Act or an ACRA administered Act at the individual's contact address is not effective to bring it to the notice of the individual`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the grounds for causing the individual's residential address to cease to be excluded from public access under section 12(2)(c) or (d) (as the case may be) are either that" (a closed list: "either ... or")

-- src:3305 | (2) Before causing the individual’s residential address to cease to be
-- src:3306 | excluded from public access pursuant to section 12E(2), the Registrar
-- src:3307 | must give a notice under subsection (3) to —
-- src:3309 | (a) the individual;
-- src:3311 | (b) every company of which the Registrar has been notified
-- src:3312 | under this Act that the individual is a director, chief
-- src:3313 | executive officer or secretary; and
-- src:3315 | (c) every private company of which the Registrar has been
-- src:3316 | notified under this Act that the individual is a member.
@ref s 12F(2) (src:3305-3316)
GIVEN `the Registrar is about to cause the individual's residential address to cease to be excluded from public access pursuant to section 12E(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company of which the Registrar has been notified under this Act that the individual is a director, chief executive officer or secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a private company of which the Registrar has been notified under this Act that the individual is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(2) the Registrar must give the person the notice under subsection (3) before causing the residential address to cease to be excluded` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Registrar is about to cause the individual's residential address to cease to be excluded from public access pursuant to section 12E(2)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before causing the individual's residential address to cease to be excluded from public access pursuant to section 12E(2), the Registrar must give a notice under subsection (3) to" (a duty gated by "Before": nothing is owed where the Registrar is not about to do so; a duty's own question; marginal reading (a))
    ELSE (IF `the person is the individual` OR `the person is a company of which the Registrar has been notified under this Act that the individual is a director, chief executive officer or secretary` OR `the person is a private company of which the Registrar has been notified under this Act that the individual is a member`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the duty runs to the individual and to the companies the paragraphs name; the text says nothing of anyone else

-- src:3320 | (3) The notice mentioned in subsection (2) must —
-- src:3322 | (a) state the grounds under subsection (1) on which the
-- src:3323 | Registrar intends to cease the exclusion of the individual’s
-- src:3324 | residential address; and
-- src:3326 | (b) specify the period within which representations may be
-- src:3327 | made to the Registrar.
@ref s 12F(3) (src:3320-3327)
GIVEN `the notice states the grounds under subsection (1) on which the Registrar intends to cause the exclusion of the individual's residential address to cease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the period within which representations may be made to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(3) the notice has the content the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the grounds under subsection (1) on which the Registrar intends to cause the exclusion of the individual's residential address to cease` AND `the notice specifies the period within which representations may be made to the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice mentioned in subsection (2) must -- (a) state the grounds under subsection (1) ...; and (b) specify the period within which representations may be made to the Registrar" (a duty not met: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- src:3329 | (4) The Registrar must consider the representations (if any) given in
-- src:3330 | response to the notice mentioned in subsection (2) and received
-- src:3331 | within the period specified by the Registrar under subsection (3)(b).
@ref s 12F(4) (src:3329-3331)
GIVEN `the representation was given in response to the notice mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the representation was received` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period the Registrar specified under subsection (3)(b)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(4) the Registrar must consider the representation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the representation was given in response to the notice mentioned in subsection (2)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to consider "the representations (if any) given in response to the notice mentioned in subsection (2)"; the text says nothing of any other representation
    ELSE (IF `the date the representation was received` AT MOST `the last day of the period the Registrar specified under subsection (3)(b)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the representations (if any) ... received within the period specified by the Registrar under subsection (3)(b)" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:3333 | (5) If the Registrar decides to cause the individual’s residential
-- src:3334 | address to cease being excluded from public access, the Registrar
-- src:3335 | must before doing so give notice of the decision to —
-- src:3337 | (a) the individual; and
-- src:3339 | (b) every company mentioned in subsection (2)(b) and (c).
@ref s 12F(5) (src:3333-3339)
GIVEN `the Registrar decides to cause the individual's residential address to cease being excluded from public access` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company mentioned in subsection (2)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(5) the Registrar must give the person notice of the decision before doing so` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Registrar decides to cause the individual's residential address to cease being excluded from public access`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Registrar decides to cause the individual's residential address to cease being excluded from public access, the Registrar must before doing so give notice of the decision to" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))
    ELSE (IF `the person is the individual` OR `the person is a company mentioned in subsection (2)(b) or (c)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the duty runs to "(a) the individual; and (b) every company mentioned in subsection (2)(b) and (c)"; the text says nothing of anyone else

-- src:3343 | (6) A notice to the individual under subsection (2) or (5) must be
-- src:3344 | sent to the individual’s residential address unless it appears to the
-- src:3345 | Registrar that service at that address may be ineffective to bring it to
-- src:3346 | the individual’s notice, in which case it may be sent to any other last
-- src:3347 | known address of that individual.
@ref s 12F(6) (src:3343-3347)
GIVEN `it appears to the Registrar that service at the individual's residential address may be ineffective to bring the notice to the individual's notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(6) the notice to the individual must be sent to the individual's residential address` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Registrar that service at the individual's residential address may be ineffective to bring the notice to the individual's notice`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be sent to the individual's residential address unless it appears to the Registrar that service at that address may be ineffective to bring it to the individual's notice" (an "unless", met)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3343 | (6) A notice to the individual under subsection (2) or (5) must be
-- src:3344 | sent to the individual’s residential address unless it appears to the
-- src:3345 | Registrar that service at that address may be ineffective to bring it to
-- src:3346 | the individual’s notice, in which case it may be sent to any other last
-- src:3347 | known address of that individual.
@ref s 12F(6) (src:3343-3347)
GIVEN `it appears to the Registrar that service at the individual's residential address may be ineffective to bring the notice to the individual's notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(6) the notice may be sent to another last known address of the individual` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Registrar that service at the individual's residential address may be ineffective to bring the notice to the individual's notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in which case it may be sent to any other last known address of that individual"; the text says nothing of the case where service at the residential address is not ineffective (the first limb of the subsection governs)

-- src:3352 | (7) Any individual aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under
-- src:3353 | section 12E(2) may, within 30 days after the date of receiving the
-- src:3354 | notice under subsection (5), appeal to the Court which may confirm
-- src:3355 | or reverse the Registrar’s decision and make any directions in the
-- src:3356 | matter.
@ref s 12F(7) (src:3352-3356)
GIVEN `the individual is aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under section 12E(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the individual received the notice under subsection (5)` IS A DATE
      `the date the appeal is brought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(7) the individual may appeal to the Court against the decision` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the individual is aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under section 12E(2)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is that of "Any individual aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under section 12E(2)"; the text says nothing of anyone else
    ELSE (IF `the date the appeal is brought` AT LEAST `the date the individual received the notice under subsection (5)` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the individual received the notice under subsection (5)` `the date the appeal is brought` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within 30 days after the date of receiving the notice under subsection (5), appeal to the Court" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); the day of receipt is in time, fork line F-H-P2)

-- src:3352 | (7) Any individual aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under
-- src:3353 | section 12E(2) may, within 30 days after the date of receiving the
-- src:3354 | notice under subsection (5), appeal to the Court which may confirm
-- src:3355 | or reverse the Registrar’s decision and make any directions in the
-- src:3356 | matter.
@ref s 12F(7) (src:3352-3356)
GIVEN `an individual aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under section 12E(2) has appealed to the Court within 30 days after the date of receiving the notice under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(7) the Court may confirm or reverse the decision of the Registrar and make any directions in the matter` MEANS
    IF `an individual aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under section 12E(2) has appealed to the Court within 30 days after the date of receiving the notice under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Court's power is on an appeal brought under this subsection; the text says nothing of any other proceeding

-- (8): "not allowed to provide a contact address within 3 years after ... unless the Registrar is satisfied that there is good cause": a bar. JUST TRUE means barred.
-- src:3358 | (8) The individual is not allowed to provide a contact address
-- src:3359 | within 3 years after the Registrar causes the individual’s residential
-- src:3360 | address to cease to be excluded from public access under
-- src:3361 | section 12(2)(c) or (d) pursuant to section 12E(2), unless the
-- src:3362 | Registrar is satisfied that there is good cause for allowing the
-- src:3363 | individual to do so in a particular case.
@ref s 12F(8) (src:3358-3363)
GIVEN `the date the Registrar caused the individual's residential address to cease to be excluded from public access pursuant to section 12E(2)` IS A DATE
      `the date the individual provides a contact address` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar is satisfied that there is good cause for allowing the individual to provide a contact address in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(8) the individual is barred from providing a contact address` MEANS
    IF `the date the individual provides a contact address` AT LEAST `the date the Registrar caused the individual's residential address to cease to be excluded from public access pursuant to section 12E(2)` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the Registrar caused the individual's residential address to cease to be excluded from public access pursuant to section 12E(2)` `the date the individual provides a contact address` 3 Years
    THEN (IF `the Registrar is satisfied that there is good cause for allowing the individual to provide a contact address in the particular case`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Registrar is satisfied that there is good cause for allowing the individual to do so in a particular case" (an "unless", met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The individual is not allowed to provide a contact address within 3 years after the Registrar causes the individual's residential address to cease to be excluded" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); the day of the cessation is inside the 3 years, fork line F-H-P2)

-- src:3367 | (9) Subject to subsection (8), where an individual provides a new
-- src:3368 | contact address under any ACRA administered Act, the Registrar
-- src:3369 | must replace the individual’s contact address contained in each
-- src:3370 | register kept by the Registrar under section 12(1) with the new
-- src:3371 | contact address.
@ref s 12F(9) (src:3367-3371)
GIVEN `the individual provides a new contact address under an ACRA administered Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (8) bars the individual from providing it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12F(9) the Registrar must replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1) with the new contact address` MEANS
    IF `the individual provides a new contact address under an ACRA administered Act` AND (NOT `subsection (8) bars the individual from providing it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (8), where an individual provides a new contact address under any ACRA administered Act, the Registrar must replace the individual's contact address" (a failed "where", or a duty "Subject to" a bar that applies: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

§ `Regulative rules of ss 12E and 12F (the Registrar's duties to the individual have no time limit and no consequence the text states, so no breach path; the individual's bar in s 12F(8) has one)`

DECLARE `s 12E and 12F act` IS ONE OF
    `s 12E(1) cause the residential address to be excluded from public access`
    `s 12E(3) cause the exclusion from public access to resume`
    `s 12E(4) cause the residential address to be excluded from public access in respect of the document`
    `s 12F(2) give the individual, and each company the paragraphs name, the notice under subsection (3)`
    `s 12F(4) consider the representations given in response to the notice`
    `s 12F(5) give notice of the decision to the individual and to each company`
    `s 12F(8) provide a contact address`
    `s 12F(9) replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1)`

-- src:3218 | 12E.—(1) The Registrar must cause —
-- src:3220 | (a) the residential address of a director, chief executive officer
-- src:3221 | or secretary contained in the register of directors, register
-- src:3222 | of chief executive officers or register of secretaries (as the
-- src:3223 | case may be) kept by the Registrar under section 173(1) to
-- src:3224 | be excluded from public access under section 12(2)(c); and
-- src:3228 | (b) the residential address of a member of a private company
-- src:3229 | (who is an individual) contained in the electronic register
-- src:3230 | of members kept by the Registrar under section 196A to be
-- src:3231 | excluded from public access under section 12(2)(d).
@ref s 12E(1) (src:3218-3231)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12E and 12F act`
`s 12E(1) rule: the Registrar's duty to exclude the residential address from public access` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 12E(1) cause the residential address to be excluded from public access`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not cause the residential address to be excluded from public access"

-- src:3245 | (3) Where, pursuant to subsection (2), the individual’s residential
-- src:3246 | address has ceased to be excluded from public access under
-- src:3251 | section 12(2)(c) or (d) (as the case may be), the Registrar must cause
-- src:3252 | the exclusion from public access to resume if —
-- src:3254 | (a) subject to section 12F(8) and the equivalent provisions in
-- src:3255 | other ACRA administered Acts, notice of a change in the
-- src:3256 | individual’s contact address is lodged under any ACRA
-- src:3257 | administered Act; or
-- src:3259 | (b) the Court so directs on an appeal under section 12F(7).
@ref s 12E(3) (src:3245-3259)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12E and 12F act`
`s 12E(3) rule: the Registrar's duty to cause the exclusion to resume` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 12E(3) cause the exclusion from public access to resume`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not cause the exclusion from public access to resume"

-- src:3263 | (4) Where —
-- src:3265 | (a) a document is filed or lodged with the Registrar under this
-- src:3266 | Act by submitting a form on the electronic transaction
-- src:3267 | system on or after the date of commencement of section 30
-- src:3268 | of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements)
-- src:3269 | Act 2024; and
-- src:3271 | (b) an individual’s residential address is entered in that form,
-- src:3273 | the Registrar must cause the individual’s residential address to be
-- src:3274 | excluded from public access in respect of that document under
-- src:3275 | section 12(2)(b).
@ref s 12E(4) (src:3263-3275)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12E and 12F act`
`s 12E(4) rule: the Registrar's duty to exclude the residential address entered in the form` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 12E(4) cause the residential address to be excluded from public access in respect of the document`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not cause the residential address entered in the form to be excluded from public access in respect of the document"

-- src:3305 | (2) Before causing the individual’s residential address to cease to be
-- src:3306 | excluded from public access pursuant to section 12E(2), the Registrar
-- src:3307 | must give a notice under subsection (3) to —
-- src:3309 | (a) the individual;
-- src:3311 | (b) every company of which the Registrar has been notified
-- src:3312 | under this Act that the individual is a director, chief
-- src:3313 | executive officer or secretary; and
-- src:3315 | (c) every private company of which the Registrar has been
-- src:3316 | notified under this Act that the individual is a member.
@ref s 12F(2) (src:3305-3316)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12E and 12F act`
`s 12F(2) rule: the Registrar's duty to give the notice under subsection (3)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 12F(2) give the individual, and each company the paragraphs name, the notice under subsection (3)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 12F(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not give the notice under subsection (3) before causing the residential address to cease to be excluded" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:3329 | (4) The Registrar must consider the representations (if any) given in
-- src:3330 | response to the notice mentioned in subsection (2) and received
-- src:3331 | within the period specified by the Registrar under subsection (3)(b).
@ref s 12F(4) (src:3329-3331)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12E and 12F act`
`s 12F(4) rule: the Registrar's duty to consider the representations` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 12F(4) consider the representations given in response to the notice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 12F(4) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not consider the representations given in response to the notice" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:3333 | (5) If the Registrar decides to cause the individual’s residential
-- src:3334 | address to cease being excluded from public access, the Registrar
-- src:3335 | must before doing so give notice of the decision to —
-- src:3337 | (a) the individual; and
-- src:3339 | (b) every company mentioned in subsection (2)(b) and (c).
@ref s 12F(5) (src:3333-3339)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12E and 12F act`
`s 12F(5) rule: the Registrar's duty to give notice of the decision` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 12F(5) give notice of the decision to the individual and to each company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 12F(5) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not give notice of the decision before causing the residential address to cease to be excluded" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:3358 | (8) The individual is not allowed to provide a contact address
-- src:3359 | within 3 years after the Registrar causes the individual’s residential
-- src:3360 | address to cease to be excluded from public access under
-- src:3361 | section 12(2)(c) or (d) pursuant to section 12E(2), unless the
-- src:3362 | Registrar is satisfied that there is good cause for allowing the
-- src:3363 | individual to do so in a particular case.
@ref s 12F(8) (src:3358-3363)
GIVEN `the name of the individual` IS A STRING
      `the number of days in the 3 years after the Registrar caused the individual's residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12E and 12F act`
`s 12F(8) rule: the individual's bar on providing a contact address` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the individual`
    SHANT `s 12F(8) provide a contact address`
    WITHIN `the number of days in the 3 years after the Registrar caused the individual's residential address to cease to be excluded from public access`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the individual` BECAUSE "the individual provided a contact address within 3 years after the Registrar caused the residential address to cease to be excluded"

-- src:3367 | (9) Subject to subsection (8), where an individual provides a new
-- src:3368 | contact address under any ACRA administered Act, the Registrar
-- src:3369 | must replace the individual’s contact address contained in each
-- src:3370 | register kept by the Registrar under section 12(1) with the new
-- src:3371 | contact address.
@ref s 12F(9) (src:3367-3371)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12E and 12F act`
`s 12F(9) rule: the Registrar's duty to replace the contact address` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 12F(9) replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1)`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1)"
